# Small quiet chips over the live view: conditions worth a sentence
# but not an interruption. These used to happen silently, which was
# the actual fault.

#. Tracking lost and the map has banked ground it could recognise:
#. the relocalizer is sweeping for it. Returning to anywhere already
#. seen recovers the position.
msgid "advice.track.searching"
msgstr "tracking lost, watching for familiar ground"

#. Tracking lost with nothing to search: the view is featureless and
#. the map has nothing banked that could be recognised.
msgid "advice.track.blank"
msgstr "tracking lost over blank glass"

#. The stage moved further between two frames than can be measured,
#. and that travel was discarded rather than guessed at.
msgid "advice.track.fast"
msgstr "moving too fast to track"

#. Offered beside "moving too fast" only when the exposure has room to
#. give: blur scales with shutter time, so this is the lever that helps.
msgid "advice.track.exposure"
msgstr "shorter exposure tracks faster motion"
